<title>USA: Northwest Air seeks to reinstate service.</title>
<headline>Northwest Air seeks to reinstate service.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northwest Airlines Corp said Tuesday it filed an application with the governments of the United States and Japan to reinstate service to Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia.</p>
<p>The carrier previously served Kuala Lumpur from 1985 to 1986. Effective July 1, Northwest plans to offer service three times weekly from Seattle to Kuala Lumpur via a stop at Osaka's Kansai International Airport.</p>
<p>It has the rights to serve Kuala Lumpur via a stop in Japan under terms of the U.S.-Japan bilateral aviation agreement.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
